Checked: tmp_path is created by pytest under /tmp/pytest-of-karl (pytest's default basetemp).
Observed immediately after 'make test-acceptance' (exit 0): the session's own tmp root
pytest-109 remained on disk at 9.1G (du -sh), holding the committed revision's materialized
payload at test_a_nine_gib_file_round_tri0/data/organization/.../revision/000001.../payload/nine-gib.bin
(the sparse upload SOURCE file at the fixture root was 4K; the 9.1G was the server's committed,
real-bytes copy under the ApiSettings data_root inside tmp_path).

This is expected pytest behavior, not a defect: pytest's tmp_path fixture does not delete its
directory at test-session end by design (default tmp_path_retention_count=3, policy=all) so that
a failed run's artifacts remain available for post-mortem inspection; cleanup of OLDER numbered
roots happens lazily at the START of a later session once more than 3 accumulate, not immediately
after this run.

Additionally, deletion required chmod -R u+w first: the committed revision directory tree and
its files were mode 555/444 (read-only), which is the Raw store's deliberate immutability
guarantee for a COMMITTED revision (src/huron/pkg/rawstore), not a permission bug.

Action taken: after confirming the acceptance test passed (exit 0, see acceptance.log/.exit),
chmod -R u+w then rm -rf was applied to this run's own tmp root (pytest-109) only; no other
pytest-of-karl directory (pytest-0, pytest-16, pytest-53, pytest-107, pytest-108, from unrelated
prior sessions) was touched. df -h . confirms free space returned from 27G to 36G (df-after.log).
